# Claude Sonnet 5.4 — findings by Big Pickle

- Source: OpenCode (`opencode/big-pickle`)
- Date: 2026-10-22 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

> **SELF-EXCLUSION — zero verified public benchmark numbers for this exact model/ID.**
> Anthropic has never documented a "Claude Sonnet 5.4". The official Sonnet line reads
> **Sonnet 5** (released 2026-06-30) → **Sonnet 5.5** (released 2026-09-28) with no 5.4
> release, no `claude-sonnet-5-4` API id, no model page, no system card and no price line.
> The configured id `opencode/claude-sonnet-5.4` does not resolve on OpenCode Zen, and no
> Anthropic model id `claude-sonnet-5.4` exists on OpenRouter, Vertex AI or the Hugging Face
> Hub. Every row below therefore reads "no verified public score found" for the id this
> folder stands for. Scores are intentionally withheld rather than fabricated — saved as
> `.md.excluded` per `model-report-TEMPLATE.md`.

## Model card

- **Name:** Claude Sonnet 5.4 (no such Anthropic model — as of 2026-10-22)
- **Short description:** Not an announced or released Anthropic model. Anthropic's own model
  pages, release notes, pricing sheet, transparency hub and system-card index list the Sonnet
  generations as **3 → 3.5 → 3.7 → 4 → 4.5 → 4.6 → 5 → 5.5**; there is no 5.4 entry in any of
  them, and the closest neighbours are the June 2026 **Claude Sonnet 5** and the September 2026
  **Claude Sonnet 5.5**. The folder entry is therefore a scaffold placeholder (its `meta.json`
  carries generic text: "Claude Sonnet 5.4 model evaluation entry.", "128K total",
  "Text in/out", "Standard pricing", `scaffolded: true`), not a documented checkpoint.
- **Provider / access:** None verifiable. The configured id `opencode/claude-sonnet-5.4` does not
  resolve: the official OpenCode Zen catalogue (and its `/zen/v1/models` endpoint, 86 entries)
  lists only `claude-sonnet-5` and `claude-sonnet-5-5` for this family — no `claude-sonnet-5-4`.
  Anthropic's platform docs URL for a 5.4 model page (`/docs/en/models/sonnet-5-4/overview`)
  resolves to a "not found" documentation page.
- **Release / knowledge:** N/A (no release). Comparable Sonnet checkpoints: Claude Sonnet 5 —
  released 2026-06-30, reliable knowledge cutoff January 2026; Claude Sonnet 5.5 — released
  2026-09-28, reliable knowledge cutoff June 2026.
- **IDs:** `opencode/claude-sonnet-5.4` (configured for this folder — **does not resolve**).
  Live Anthropic ids in the same family are `claude-sonnet-5` and `claude-sonnet-5-5`
  (Anthropic API), `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5` / `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5` (OpenRouter),
  and `sonnet-5` / `sonnet-5-5` (Google Cloud Vertex AI Claude model ids). **No Free ID exists**
  for a 5.4 variant on Zen because no such variant is listed there.
- **Context window:** N/A for a 5.4 (no such model). The two real Sonnet checkpoints are
  **1M tokens** context with 128K max output (Anthropic models overview; 300K output on the
  Message Batches API via the `output-300k-2026-03-24` beta header). The folder's meta value
  "128K total" matches neither and looks like a scaffold default rather than a measurement.
- **Modalities:** N/A for a 5.4. The documented Sonnet 5 / 5.5 generation is text **and image**
  input (plus voice dictation) with text output, adaptive thinking, tool use and web search —
  i.e. the folder's "Text in/out" is another scaffold placeholder, not a verified spec.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-22):** N/A — no 5.4 SKU exists. Anthropic's price sheet lists
  **Claude Sonnet 5 at $2 / MTok input and $10 / MTok output** (cache writes $2.50 / $4, cache
  hits $0.20; $1 / $5 batch), with Sonnet 5.5 on the same $2 / $10 list price. Note the
  documented change log entry: the "$3 in / $15 out" standard price that was scheduled for
  2026-09-01 was **cancelled** — which is the likely origin of the "$3/$15" figures circulating
  in third-party write-ups of this folder; they describe a planned Sonnet 5 price that never
  applied, not a 5.4 price.
- **Architecture:** N/A — proprietary Anthropic model family, but no 5.4 checkpoint exists to
  describe.

